{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"identifier","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"UnsafePointer","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SP"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gchar","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"gchar"},{"text":">? = nil)","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifier"},{"text":" can either be an RFC3339\/ISO 8601 time offset or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"something that would pass as a valid value for the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TZ"},{"text":" environment","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"variable (including ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In Windows, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" can also be the unlocalized name of a time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"zone for standard time, for example “Pacific Standard Time”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Valid RFC3339 time offsets are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"Z\""},{"text":" (for UTC) or","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"\"±hh:mm\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":".  ISO 8601 additionally specifies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"\"±hhmm\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"±hh\""},{"text":".  Offsets are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"time values to be added to Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) to get"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the local time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In UNIX, the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TZ"},{"type":"text","text":" environment variable typically corresponds"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the name of a file in the zoneinfo database, an absolute path to a file","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"somewhere else, or a string in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“std offset [dst [offset],start[\/time],end[\/time]]” (POSIX) format."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"There  are  no spaces in the specification. The name of standard"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and daylight savings time zone must be three or more alphabetic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"characters. Offsets are time values to be added to local time to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"get Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) and should be"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"[±]hh[[:]mm[:ss]]\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".  Dates are either","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"Jn\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (Julian day with n between 1 and 365, leap"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"years not counted), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"n\""},{"type":"text","text":" (zero-based Julian day"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with n between 0 and 365) or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"Mm.w.d\""},{"type":"text","text":" (day d"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(0 <= d <= 6) of week w (1 <= w <= 5) of month m (1 <= m <= 12), day","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"0 is a Sunday).  Times are in local wall clock time, the default is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"02:00:00.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In Windows, the “tzn[+|–]hh","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"#dzn"},{"type":"text","text":"” format is used, but also"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accepts POSIX format.  The Windows format uses US rules for all time","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zones; daylight savings time is 60 minutes behind the standard time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"with date and time of change taken from Pacific Standard Time.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Offsets are time values to be added to the local time to get"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Coordinated Universal Time (UTC).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"g_time_zone_new_local()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" calls this function with the value of the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"TZ","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" environment variable. This function itself is independent of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the value of "},{"code":"TZ","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but if ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifier"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/etc\/localtime"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"will be consulted to discover the correct time zone on UNIX and the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"registry will be consulted or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GetTimeZoneInformation()"},{"type":"text","text":" will be used"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"to get the local time zone on Windows."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If intervals are not available, only time zone rules from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TZ"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"environment variable or other means, then they will be computed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from year 1900 to 2037.  If the maximum year for the rules is"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"available and it is greater than 2037, then it will followed"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"instead."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"http:\/\/tools.ietf.org\/html\/rfc3339#section-5.6"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for a precise definition of valid RFC3339 time offsets","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"(the "},{"code":"time-offset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" expansion) and ISO 8601 for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full list of valid time offsets.  See","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"http:\/\/www.gnu.org\/s\/libc\/manual\/html_node\/TZ-Variable.html","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"for an explanation of the possible"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values of the "},{"code":"TZ","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" environment variable. See"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"http:\/\/msdn.microsoft.com\/en-us\/library\/ms912391%28v=winembedded.11%29.aspx","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"for the list of time zones on Windows.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You should release the return value by calling ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_time_zone_unref()"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"when you are done with it."}]}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"init","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UnsafePointer"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gchar","text":"gchar"},{"text":">?)","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"roleHeading":"Initializer","extendedModule":"GLib","externalID":"s:4GLib11TimeZoneRefV10identifierACSPys4Int8VGSg_tcfc","title":"init(identifier:)"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/timezoneref\/init(identifier:)"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneRef\/init(identifier:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneRef"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZone","isActive":true},{"text":" corresponding to ","type":"text"},{"code":"identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"code":"identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cannot be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"parsed or loaded, "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is returned."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/TimeZoneRef/init(identifier:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"identifier","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnsafePointer","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SP"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"text":"gchar","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gchar"},{"text":">?)","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/timezoneref\/init(identifier:)","title":"init(identifier:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZone"},{"type":"text","text":" corresponding to "},{"code":"identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"parsed or loaded, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" is returned."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneRef\/init(identifier:)"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/TimeZone":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TimeZone","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"GTimeZone","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" represents a time zone, at no particular point in time.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZone","title":"TimeZone","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"TimeZone","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/timezone","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3339#section-5.6":{"identifier":"http:\/\/tools.ietf.org\/html\/rfc3339#section-5.6","title":"RFC3339 §5.6","url":"http:\/\/tools.ietf.org\/html\/rfc3339#section-5.6","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"RFC3339 §5.6"}]},"#dzn":{"identifier":"#dzn","title":":mm[:ss]","url":"#dzn","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":":mm[:ss]"}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/TimeZoneRef":{"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/timezoneref","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimeZoneRef"}],"role":"symbol","title":"TimeZoneRef","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"GTimeZone","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" represents a time zone, at no particular point in time.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimeZoneRef"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/TimeZoneRef","type":"topic"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","title":"GLib","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/ms912391%28v=winembedded.